I have completed the task `lucebox-hub-gfx1151-vnt`. The root cause of the `tria_k_pre_rope` pointer corruption was a CMake issue - the `DFLASH27B_TRIATTENTION_ENABLED` compile definition was only set on the `dflash27b` library, not on test executables. This caused a struct layout mismatch between the library (which had the `tria_k_pre_rope` field) and the test code (which didn't).

**Fix summary:**
1. Added `DFLASH27B_TRIATTENTION_ENABLED=1` to `test_dflash`, `test_generate`, `smoke_target_forward`, `smoke_laguna_forward`, `bench_laguna_ttft`, `bench_laguna_pflash`, `bench_laguna_generate`
2. Added `deps/llama.cpp/triattention` to `DFLASH27B_SRC_INCLUDE_DIRS` for the header include
3. Reduced debug log verbosity for better performance

**Verification:**
- `[TriAttention] build_full_attn_block tria_k_pre_rope=0x41523be0 data=0xd8f72ba2000 ne=[256,4096,4]` - valid heap address
- test_dflash e2e inference: 20 tokens generated successfully
- Output decodable (valid token IDs)
